+    // inu: Telegram's translate endpoint only accepts a BATCH of texts from a Premium account; a
+    // free account has to send them one at a time or the whole request comes back refused. That is
+    // the actual reason the chat translate bar translated nothing without Premium while the
+    // single-message menu worked fine - the bar batches, the menu does not. Cherrygram handles it
+    // the same way (TelegramTranslator: `int maxSize = isPremium() ? 20 : 1`). No toggle: there is
+    // no sane reason to want a batch size that the server will reject.
+    // Compared as `size() + 1 >= limit`, exactly like stock, so the Premium path stays
+    // byte-for-byte stock behaviour and only the free path changes.
